                    "value": "Source: USGS earthquake feed, all magnitudes for the last 30 days, collected every 15 minutes into a local PostgreSQL database. USGS lists small earthquakes mostly in the US, so global comparisons are most reliable at magnitude 4 and above. The tsunami flag is set for large earthquakes in oceanic regions; it does not mean a tsunami happened or a warning was issued. PAGER alerts estimate impact from green (low) to red (high).",
